          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em parameterized spectrum
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            (
            %a{:href => "#MaySigurdsson06"}> May-Sigurdsson 06
            ), hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+homotopy+theory"} parameterized homotopy theory
          %p
            Specifically, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            thought of as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is equivalently an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Spec
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \longrightarrow Spec
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (∞,1)-category of spectra
            (
            %a{:href => "#AndoBlumbergGepner11"}> Ando-Blumberg-Gepner 11
            ): this assigns to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
            of spectra, to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            between such equivalences, and so forth.
          %p
            More generally, given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\mathbf{H}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            parameterized over any object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+locus"} Joyal locus
          %p
            The intrinsic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            of parameterized spectra is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+generalized+cohomology"} twisted generalized cohomology
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+bivariant+cohomology"} twisted bivariant cohomology
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            For more see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_comodule_spectra As (co)module spectra
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a connected homotopy type, then the
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+%E2%88%9E-ring"} ∞-group ∞-ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[\Omega X]
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            corresponding to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
          %p
            To see this, use first that
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-functors"} ∞-functors
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Spectra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \Omega X \longrightarrow Spectra
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            out of the one-object spectrum enriched
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[\Omega X] \simeq \Sigma^\infty_+ \Omega X
          %p
            Moreover
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[\Omega X]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
            are equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodule+spectra"} comodule spectra
            over the coalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[X] = \Sigma^\infty_+ X
            induced from the
            %span.newWikiWord
              coalgebra object
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/coalgebra+object"} ?
            structure of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} Cartesian monoidal (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            (
            %a{:href => "cartesian+monoidal+infinity%2C1-category#CoalgebraObjects"}> here
            ), and using that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CoModSpectra
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ModSpectra
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CoModSpectra_{\mathbb{S}[X]}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  ModSpectra_{\mathbb{S}[\Omega X]}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HessShipley14"}> Hess-Shipley 14, theorem 1.2 with prop. 5.18
            )
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-theory"} A-theory
          %h3#SixOperationsYoga Six operations yoga
          %p
            For any map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\longrightarrow Y
            between
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wirthm%C3%BCller+context"} Wirthmüller context
            version of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/yoga+of+six+functors"} yoga of six functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X,Spectra]
                  \\stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  [Y,Spectra]
          %p
            in that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            is not only a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            but also a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+closed+functor"} strong closed functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            holds.
          %p
            Moreover, along (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"}> co-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spans"} spans
            of morphisms pull-push
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_!\dashv f^\ast)
